# Portfolio Skill

## Purpose

This skill is for building a personal developer portfolio primarily as a learning and project-showcase website.

The portfolio should present the developer's projects, technical learning, experiments, architecture decisions, and development progress in a clear and credible way.

if you want to add time elasped for this portfolio you can run `scripts/time.js`

The main reference projects are:

- `auth` — Authentication and authorization learning project
- `buildforms` — Dynamic form-builder learning project
- `knowstack` — AI-powered knowledge/RAG learning project
- `poll-platform` — Polling and voting platform learning project

These projects are primarily intended to demonstrate learning, engineering ability, experimentation, and understanding of modern software architecture.

---

## When to use this skill

Use this skill when:

- Building or modifying the personal portfolio
- Adding a project to the portfolio
- Writing project descriptions
- Creating project case studies
- Explaining project architecture
- Documenting technical decisions
- Adding skills or technologies
- Creating a project detail page
- Improving portfolio UI/UX
- Writing learning outcomes
- Creating a project timeline
- Presenting GitHub or demo links
- Improving portfolio responsiveness
- Adding animations or interactions
- Improving SEO or accessibility
- Organizing projects into categories

