# Reference Projects

## 1. Auth

### Purpose

An authentication and authorization learning project focused on understanding modern authentication architecture.

### Areas of learning

- OAuth 2.0
- OpenID Connect
- JWT
- Sessions
- Identity providers
- Authentication callbacks
- Protected routes
- Authorization
- Token validation
- Security considerations

### Portfolio positioning

Present this project as an exploration of how authentication systems work internally and how different authentication mechanisms fit together.

Example description:

> A learning project focused on understanding and implementing modern authentication flows using OAuth 2.0, OpenID Connect, tokens, sessions, and protected routes.

---

# 2. BuildForms

### Purpose

A learning project for understanding how dynamic form-builder systems can be designed and implemented.

### Areas of learning

- Dynamic form schemas
- Form rendering
- Reusable fields
- Validation
- Conditional fields
- Form submissions
- API design
- Database modeling
- Type-safe form configuration

### Portfolio positioning

Focus on the engineering challenge of designing a flexible system rather than simply describing it as a form application.

Example description:

> A learning project exploring how to design a schema-driven form builder with reusable fields, validation, conditional logic, and dynamic form rendering.

---

# 3. KnowStack

### Purpose

An AI and knowledge-system learning project focused on understanding how information can be collected, indexed, retrieved, and used by AI systems.

### Areas of learning

- Document ingestion
- Web content ingestion
- YouTube content
- Chunking
- Embeddings
- Vector search
- Semantic search
- RAG
- Source citations
- AI agents
- Retrieval pipelines
- Context construction

### Portfolio positioning

Present KnowStack as an exploration of AI knowledge systems and retrieval architecture.

Example description:

> A learning project exploring how AI-powered knowledge systems can ingest information from multiple sources, retrieve relevant context, and generate source-aware answers using RAG and AI agents.

---

# 4. Poll Platform

### Purpose

A learning project for understanding how polling and voting systems can be designed with reliable data handling and real-time results.

### Areas of learning

- Poll creation
- Questions and options
- Voting
- Duplicate vote prevention
- Validation
- Poll lifecycle
- Results
- Analytics
- API design
- Database consistency
- Real-time updates

### Portfolio positioning

Focus on learning about state, consistency, concurrency, and data modeling.

Example description:

> A learning project exploring how to build a polling platform with voting, validation, result aggregation, participation tracking, and scalable backend architecture.

